1
00:00:00,199 --> 00:00:04,320
soon forgot their existence.

2
00:00:04,320 --> 00:00:08,639
The mystery of where the milk went to was soon cleared up.

3
00:00:08,639 --> 00:00:12,559
It was mixed every day into the pigs' mash.

4
00:00:12,559 --> 00:00:19,199
The early apples were now ripening and the grass of the orchard was littered with windfalls.

5
00:00:19,199 --> 00:00:24,960
The animals had assumed, as a matter of course, that these would be shared out equally.

6
00:00:24,960 --> 00:00:30,000
One day, however, the order went forth that all the windfalls were to be

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,599
collected and brought to the harness room for the use of the pigs.

8
00:00:35,599 --> 00:00:41,320
At this, some of the other animals murmured, but it was no use.

9
00:00:41,320 --> 00:00:47,360
All the pigs were in full agreement on this point, even Snowball and Napoleon.

10
00:00:47,360 --> 00:00:52,000
Squealer was sent to make the necessary explanations to the others.

11
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:56,480
>> Comrades, you do not imagine, I hope, that we pigs are doing this in a spirit

12
00:00:56,480 --> 00:01:01,559
of selfishness and privilege. Many of us actually dislike milk and apples. I

13
00:01:01,559 --> 00:01:07,039
dislike them myself. Our sole object in taking these things is to preserve our

14
00:01:07,039 --> 00:01:12,639
health. Milk and apples, this has been proved by science, comrades, contains

15
00:01:12,639 --> 00:01:18,719
substances absolutely necessary to the well-being of a pig. We pigs are brain

16
00:01:18,719 --> 00:01:24,320
workers. The whole management and organization of this farm depend on us.

17
00:01:24,320 --> 00:01:29,280
Day and night, we are watching over your welfare. It is for your sake that we

18
00:01:29,280 --> 00:01:34,239
drink that milk and eat those apples. Do you know what would happen if we pigs

19
00:01:34,239 --> 00:01:36,159
failed in our duty?

20
00:01:36,159 --> 00:01:43,199
Jones would come back. Yes, Jones would come back. Surely, comrades,

21
00:01:43,199 --> 00:01:49,000
>> cried Squealer almost pleadingly, skipping from side to side and whisking his tail.

22
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:53,760
>> Surely, there is no one among you who wants to see Jones come back.

23
00:01:53,760 --> 00:01:58,159
>> Now, if there was one thing that the animals were completely certain of, it

24
00:01:58,159 --> 00:02:02,039
was that they did not want Jones back.

25
00:02:02,039 --> 00:02:06,559
When it was put to them in this light, they had no more to say.

26
00:02:06,559 --> 00:02:11,880
The importance of keeping the pigs in good health was all too obvious.

27
00:02:11,880 --> 00:02:16,360
So, it was agreed, without further argument, that the milk and the windfall

28
00:02:16,360 --> 00:02:19,000
